{
  "$comment": [
    "Helpdesk wire contract between Portal and Admin (BackOffice). v1 was captured from a real local run of both apps on 2026-10-28 and anonymised; v2 (tickets-v2-figma-addendum.md §2/§4a, 2026-10-28) adds the flag, the student-timeline filters, aiAssist, the FAQ reads and the suggest source. v3 (helpdesk-agent-v2-pi-dsh, 2026-10-29) adds the suggest runId / parentRunId and the W3C traceparent header Portal sends on every Admin helpdesk call. v4 (helpdesk-v3-alternatives-rating, 2026-10-29) adds the suggest alternatives (\"You might be asking\": 0-3 { faqId, question }, only when suggestion is null, [] when rate limited) and the learner's rating (1-5 or null) of each aiAssist answer; the first aiAssist item carries a rating (4) so both sides compare a number. v5 (helpdesk-v4-order-and-chat-end Part A, 2026-10-29) adds the enquiry's order: orderId (string or null) on every list and detail ticket, and detail.order, a read-only projection Portal builds by code from the learner's own order record ({ id, status, amount (minor units), currency, planName, kind, createdAt, paymentMode }, nothing else; null without an order), with the orderStatus, orderKind and paymentMode enums Admin labels. The suggest requests are unchanged: the AI agent never receives order data. v6 (helpdesk-v5-context-chips-and-smalltalk Parts A/B/D/H and helpdesk-v5-faq-graph-design, 2026-10-30, all additive) adds: the situation-signal enums (situationSignal: what Portal computes by code from its own stores, never sent to Admin or the model; faqSignal: the tags an FAQ can carry, in chip priority order) and signals on every public FAQ; the FAQ question-tree release Portal caches (GET /api/integration/helpdesk/faq-release/current?locale=, bearer, ETag \"v<version>\", If-None-Match -> 304, 404 no_release before the first release) with answer|choice nodes, follow_up|option edges (labels resolved) and answer blocks b1..bn split by code at release time; the suggest request's context { nodeId?, sessionId?, recentTurns? (learner text only, at most 3) }, sent only by a v6 Portal; and, only when the request carries context, the suggest answer's kind (answer|smalltalk|clarify|no_match), intent, confidence (sure|unsure), nodeId, blocks, opening, closing, reply, explanation, covered, guard ({ result: passed|fallback, reason, fallback }) and releaseVersion. A request without context gets exactly the v5 answer, so an old Portal is unaffected; an old Admin ignores context.",
    "Identical copies live in learningguideportal/tests/fixtures/helpdesk-contract.json, learningguideadmin/server/src/backoffice/tests/fixtures/helpdesk-contract.json and learningguideadmin/client/tests/fixtures/helpdesk-contract.json.",
    "Change all copies together; each repo's tests check its own side against this file."
  ],
